                                    <h1>Website Development Cost in India 2026 &mdash; Honest Pricing Guide (Real Ranges, Hidden Costs)</h1>
                                    <p><strong>Short answer:</strong> a real business website in India in 2026 costs <strong>&#8377;1.5L&ndash;&#8377;5L</strong> for a 5&ndash;15 page site with custom design and SEO setup. A landing page is <strong>&#8377;15K&ndash;&#8377;60K</strong>. A custom website with deep integrations or unique UX is <strong>&#8377;3L&ndash;&#8377;15L</strong>. An e-commerce store is <strong>&#8377;2L&ndash;&#8377;15L</strong>. An enterprise web platform is <strong>&#8377;15L&ndash;&#8377;60L+</strong>. Below these ranges you&rsquo;re paying for a template hack-job; above them you&rsquo;re paying for an agency&rsquo;s overhead, not better engineering.</p><p>This is the cost guide we give Indian founders evaluating quotes. Real ranges from 300+ websites we&rsquo;ve shipped, the page-by-page math, hidden costs that don&rsquo;t make it into headline quotes, and an honest framework for &lsquo;is this quote fair?&rsquo;.</p>

                                    <h2>TL;DR &mdash; What a Website <em>Actually</em> Costs in India in 2026</h2>

                                    <table class="cmp-table"><thead><tr><th>Type</th><th>Cost (INR)</th><th>USD equivalent</th><th>Timeline</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Landing page</strong></td><td>&#8377;15K &ndash; &#8377;60K</td><td>$180 &ndash; $720</td><td>1&ndash;2 weeks</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Business website (5&ndash;15 pages)</strong></td><td class="win">&#8377;1.5L &ndash; &#8377;5L</td><td>$1,800 &ndash; $6,000</td><td>4&ndash;8 weeks</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Custom website (deep integrations / unique UX)</strong></td><td>&#8377;3L &ndash; &#8377;15L</td><td>$3,600 &ndash; $18,000</td><td>2&ndash;4 months</td></tr><tr><td><strong>E-commerce store (Shopify / WooCommerce)</strong></td><td>&#8377;2L &ndash; &#8377;15L</td><td>$2,400 &ndash; $18,000</td><td>3&ndash;14 weeks</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Enterprise web platform / multi-region</strong></td><td>&#8377;15L &ndash; &#8377;60L+</td><td>$18K &ndash; $72K+</td><td>4&ndash;9 months</td></tr></tbody></table><p>These are senior-led India studio rates in 2026 with 100% source-code ownership. Below this range is template-shop territory where you pay less but get less. Above this range is US/EU agency pricing (3&ndash;5&times; higher for comparable scope) where you&rsquo;re paying for agency overhead, not better engineering.</p>

                                    <h2>Page-by-page cost math &mdash; how we quote a website</h2>

                                    <p>Most agencies quote total project cost. We quote per-page cost so you can see exactly what you&rsquo;re paying for:</p><table class="cmp-table"><thead><tr><th>Component</th><th>Cost (INR)</th><th>What&rsquo;s included</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Custom design (homepage)</td><td>&#8377;40K &ndash; &#8377;1L</td><td>UX wireframe, visual design, mobile design</td></tr><tr><td>Custom design (interior page)</td><td>&#8377;15K &ndash; &#8377;30K</td><td>Per template type (about, services, contact)</td></tr><tr><td>Frontend build (per template)</td><td>&#8377;15K &ndash; &#8377;30K</td><td>HTML/CSS/JS, responsive, animations</td></tr><tr><td>CMS setup &amp; integration</td><td>&#8377;25K &ndash; &#8377;75K</td><td>WordPress / Next.js + headless CMS, content modelling</td></tr><tr><td>Forms + Zapier / CRM integration</td><td>&#8377;10K &ndash; &#8377;30K</td><td>Form-to-CRM (HubSpot / Zoho / etc), spam filtering</td></tr><tr><td>SEO setup (per site)</td><td>&#8377;25K &ndash; &#8377;60K</td><td>On-page, schema, sitemap, robots, Search Console</td></tr><tr><td>Performance optimisation</td><td>&#8377;20K &ndash; &#8377;50K</td><td>Core Web Vitals, image optimisation, CDN setup</td></tr><tr><td>Analytics + tracking setup</td><td>&#8377;15K &ndash; &#8377;40K</td><td>GA4, GTM, conversion goals, custom events</td></tr><tr><td>Content writing (per page)</td><td>&#8377;5K &ndash; &#8377;15K</td><td>SEO-optimised copy if not provided</td></tr><tr><td>QA + UAT + handover</td><td>&#8377;15K &ndash; &#8377;40K</td><td>Cross-browser test, accessibility audit, training</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Add up the line items for the scope you need and you&rsquo;ve got a fair quote. Most agencies bundle these into a single price, which is fine &mdash; but if you can&rsquo;t back-calculate the math, the agency&rsquo;s margin is opaque.</p>

                                    <h2>The 5 hidden costs that don&rsquo;t make it into the headline quote</h2>

                                    <p>The build is one cost. The full year-1 picture:</p><ol><li><strong>Hosting:</strong> &#8377;1.5K&ndash;&#8377;25K/month depending on scale. Shared hosting (HostGator, BigRock) is cheap but slow. Cloud (AWS Lightsail, GCP, DigitalOcean) is what serious sites use.</li><li><strong>Domain + SSL:</strong> &#8377;1K&ndash;&#8377;3K/year for domain, free SSL via Let&rsquo;s Encrypt (most hosting bundles it).</li><li><strong>CDN + performance services:</strong> Cloudflare free tier covers most sites; paid (&#8377;1.5K&ndash;&#8377;15K/month) for high-traffic.</li><li><strong>Backups + security:</strong> Wordfence, ManageWP, UpdraftPlus &mdash; &#8377;500&ndash;&#8377;5K/month. Critical for WordPress.</li><li><strong>Ongoing content updates + small changes:</strong> Either a small AMC retainer (&#8377;8K&ndash;&#8377;25K/month for 5&ndash;15 hours of changes) or per-change billing (&#8377;1500&ndash;&#8377;5K per change). Plan for this from day 1.</li></ol><p>Total realistic year-1 cost = build cost + 10&ndash;20%. Plan for that on day one. The agencies that quote without mentioning year-1 ops are setting you up for surprises.</p>

                                    <h2>WordPress, custom code, Webflow &mdash; honest comparison</h2>

                                    <table class="cmp-table"><thead><tr><th>Path</th><th>Build cost</th><th>Year-1 ops</th><th>Best for</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Webflow / no-code</strong></td><td>&#8377;30K &ndash; &#8377;3L</td><td>&#8377;1K &ndash; &#8377;3K/mo (Webflow plan)</td><td>Pre-launch, brochure, founders without dev team. Fast launch, limited customisation.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>WordPress + custom theme</strong></td><td class="win">&#8377;1.5L &ndash; &#8377;6L</td><td>&#8377;3K &ndash; &#8377;15K/mo</td><td>Content-heavy, blog-heavy, multilingual sites. Mature plugin ecosystem.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Custom code (Next.js / Laravel)</strong></td><td>&#8377;3L &ndash; &#8377;15L+</td><td>&#8377;5K &ndash; &#8377;30K/mo</td><td>Performance-critical, unique workflows, deep integrations. Long-term ownership.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Shopify / WooCommerce e-com</strong></td><td>&#8377;2L &ndash; &#8377;15L</td><td>&#8377;5K &ndash; &#8377;25K/mo</td><td>D2C brands. Shopify for under $5M ARR, custom headless above.</td></tr></tbody></table><div class="verdict"><strong>Honest framework:</strong> Webflow if launching this month. WordPress for content-heavy sites with cheap ongoing maintenance. Custom code for performance-critical or unique-workflow sites. We&rsquo;ll tell you which fits &mdash; even if the answer is &ldquo;don&rsquo;t hire us, use Webflow for 6 months.&rdquo;</div>

                                    <h2>Cost by industry &mdash; what affects the build price</h2>

                                    <p>Same scope, different industry = different cost. Industry-specific factors:</p><ul><li><strong>D2C / e-commerce:</strong> &#8377;2L&ndash;&#8377;15L. Cost driver: catalog size, payment + shipping integration, conversion engineering.</li><li><strong>Real estate (project microsite):</strong> &#8377;1.5L&ndash;&#8377;6L. Cost driver: virtual tour embeds, lead-capture forms, brochure delivery.</li><li><strong>Healthcare (clinic / hospital):</strong> &#8377;1.5L&ndash;&#8377;8L. Cost driver: appointment booking, ABDM compliance, multi-doctor scheduling.</li><li><strong>Education (school / coaching):</strong> &#8377;1.5L&ndash;&#8377;6L. Cost driver: admission flow, fee payment, course catalog, parent portal.</li><li><strong>SaaS / B2B (marketing site):</strong> &#8377;2L&ndash;&#8377;8L. Cost driver: conversion engineering, demo booking, lead-capture optimisation.</li><li><strong>Logistics / B2B services:</strong> &#8377;1.5L&ndash;&#8377;5L. Cost driver: corporate-form complexity, multi-stakeholder portal needs.</li><li><strong>Manufacturer corporate site:</strong> &#8377;1.5L&ndash;&#8377;6L. Cost driver: product catalog depth, RFQ flow, dealer locator.</li><li><strong>Finance / NBFC compliance-aware site:</strong> &#8377;2L&ndash;&#8377;8L. Cost driver: KYC flow, compliance copy, calculator embeds, lead routing.</li></ul>

                                    <h2>Red flags in cheap quotes</h2>

                                    <p>If a Mumbai agency is quoting your business website at &#8377;25K&ndash;&#8377;60K total &mdash; here&rsquo;s what you&rsquo;re not getting:</p><ul><li><strong>No custom design.</strong> They&rsquo;ll buy a ThemeForest template, swap your logo, hand it over. Looks like 50,000 other sites.</li><li><strong>No SEO setup.</strong> You&rsquo;ll launch invisible to Google. Add &#8377;25K&ndash;&#8377;60K later to fix it.</li><li><strong>No mobile design.</strong> Mobile is &ldquo;handled by responsive theme&rdquo; &mdash; meaning untested, often broken.</li><li><strong>No proper CMS.</strong> Often Wix or hardcoded HTML. You can&rsquo;t add a blog post without paying them.</li><li><strong>No source-code ownership.</strong> They keep the hosting + CMS access. You can&rsquo;t move providers without buying the assets later.</li><li><strong>No QA or training.</strong> You discover bugs after launch, fix-billing starts.</li></ul><p>The total bill ends up higher than just paying &#8377;1.5L upfront. Cheap is expensive when it comes to websites.</p>

                                    <div style="background:linear-gradient(135deg,#0d47a1,#1565c0);padding:40px;border-radius:12px;margin:40px 0;text-align:center;color:#fff;">
