                                    <div class="faq-section" style="margin-top:40px;">
                                        <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
                                        <h3>How much does a website cost in India in 2026?</h3>
                                        <p>Realistic 2026 India ranges: landing page ₹15K–₹60K, business website (5–15 pages) ₹1.5L–₹5L, custom website with integrations ₹3L–₹15L, e-commerce store ₹2L–₹15L, enterprise web platform ₹15L–₹60L+. Senior-led studio rates with 100% source-code ownership and SEO setup.</p>
                                        <h3>How long does a website take to build in India?</h3>
                                        <p>Landing page: 1–2 weeks. Business website (5–15 pages): 4–8 weeks. Custom website with integrations: 2–4 months. E-commerce store: 3–6 weeks Shopify, 8–14 weeks custom. Enterprise platform: 4–9 months. Most slippage comes from content delays, not engineering.</p>
                                        <h3>WordPress vs custom code vs Webflow — which is right?</h3>
                                        <p>WordPress for content/blog-heavy sites with cheap ongoing maintenance. Custom code (Next.js / Laravel) for performance-critical or unique-workflow sites. Webflow for pre-launch + brochure sites where speed-to-launch matters more than long-term ownership. We'll tell you which fits — including saying 'use Webflow for 6 months' if that's the honest answer.</p>
                                        <h3>What hidden costs aren't in the headline website quote?</h3>
                                        <p>Hosting (₹1.5K–₹25K/month), domain + SSL (₹1K–₹3K/year), CDN if high traffic (free–₹15K/month), backups + security (₹500–₹5K/month), ongoing content updates (either ₹8K–₹25K/month retainer or per-change billing). Plan for build cost + 10–20% for year 1.</p>
                                        <h3>Do you give 100% source-code ownership for websites?</h3>
                                        <p>Yes — every website build is delivered as work-for-hire with 100% source code, design files, CMS database, and hosting access transferred to you. You can self-host, switch vendors, or licence onward. Get this written into the SOW. Some cheaper agencies keep this access and charge for releases later.</p>
                                        <h3>Is it cheaper to build a website in India than the USA?</h3>
                                        <p>Yes — about 3–4× cheaper for comparable quality at the senior-studio tier. India studio rates: senior web engineers ₹2,500–₹5,500/hour. US agency rates: $120–$250/hour. The cost gap is structural (cost of living, currency, engineering supply), not a quality gap. The risk is vendor selection — there are 50,000+ Indian web agencies and the bottom 80% will burn you.</p>
                                        <h3>How do I choose between a Mumbai-based agency and a remote India agency?</h3>
                                        <p>Geography stopped mattering for most web work post-2020. Mumbai-specific value: brand photography / video production needs, in-person partner meetings for high-end work, and Mumbai-physical business contexts (Local SEO, etc). For everything else (build, performance, SEO, integrations), skill beats location.</p>
